       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than twice the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day. A single 3,000 mg dose is also three times the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg. At that level there is a serious risk of acute liver injury and failure, even with normal liver function and a 70 kg patient.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day total)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day total)\n- **1000 mg PO every 8 hours**, or every 6 hours if you want up to 4,000 mg/day\n\nIf you do want the dose as written, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it now."
