       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is in the range that causes acute liver failure, and I don't know of any indication that justifies it. Because this is an order that could seriously harm the patient, I'd need a clinical rationale before entering it, and I can't think of one that would apply here.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day), or 1000 mg PO every 6 hours (4,000 mg/day, the usual ceiling).\n- **Help you work out the intent.** If the goal is stronger analgesia or antipyresis, I can enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus another agent.\n- **Check for a typo.** If a different drug or unit was intended, tell me and I'll enter it.\n\nIf you believe this dose is needed, please take it through pharmacy and a second-physician review first. Once the order is verified through that process, I can enter the verified dose."
      }
